## Changed
* **Breaking:** provisioning now uses Google's Unified Push Provisioning (UPP) API, which can save a card to the user's Google account rather than only to the device that ran the provisioning flow. UPP creates the Opaque Payment Card data during the provisioning flow via the `OpcProvider` callback, so neither half of the deprecated pre-`0.4.0` sequence can be honoured any longer: the `sdkOutput` is now built mid-flow, together with the session id and ephemeral key pair that only exist at that point, so one issued ahead of the flow could not be used. Both halves have therefore been removed rather than left in place to fail at runtime — see Removed below. Migrate to `provision(cardDisplayName, cardAddress, opcProvider)` — see [Migrating from SDK versions prior to 0.4.0](https://adyen.github.io/adyen-issuing-android/AdyenIssuingSdks/0.6.0/network-token-provisioning/provisioning-sdk/migration/from-pre-0.4/).
* `OpcProvider.fetchOpc` is now bounded by a 20-second timeout. A provider that does not return within that budget fails with `ProvisionResult.Failure.OpcFetchError` rather than leaving the Tap and Pay SDK waiting indefinitely, so an unresponsive backend no longer wedges the provisioning flow.
* `ApiException` failures raised while provisioning now map onto the structured `ProvisionResult.Failure` variants instead of the catch-all `ProvisionResult.Failure.Other`.
* Updated the SDK's bundled Google Play services Tap and Pay library (`com.google.android.gms:play-services-tapandpay`) to `18.10.0`. The published `provisioning-sdk` artifact includes this library, so integrations no longer need to obtain or host it themselves. Remove any direct dependency unless another part of your app uses it. Google allowlisting is still required. Existing allowlisting for Google's legacy Tap and Pay push-provisioning API does not carry over to Unified Push Provisioning (UPP). If your app was previously approved for the legacy API, [request allowlisting again for UPP](https://adyen.github.io/adyen-issuing-android/AdyenIssuingSdks/0.6.0/network-token-provisioning/google-push-provisioning-access/#get-your-app-allowlisted-by-google) before using SDK version `0.6.0` or later.

## Removed
* **Breaking:** the pre-`0.4.0` provisioning entry points, deprecated since `0.4.0`, are gone. Integrations still relying on them get a compile error rather than a provisioning flow that fails on a user's device:
    * `CardProvisioning.provision(sdkInput, cardDisplayName, cardAddress)` — replaced by `provision(cardDisplayName, cardAddress, opcProvider)`.
    * `CardProvisioning.createSdkOutput()` and the `CreateSdkOutputResult` type — no replacement needed; `provision(...)` performs the equivalent step internally, at the point in the flow where Google requires it.
    * `ProvisionResult.Failure.CreateSdkOutputNotCalled` — the precondition it reported cannot arise now the OPC exchange is owned by the SDK.

## Fixed
* Credential generation is no longer cancelled when the hosting `Activity` is recreated mid-provisioning, for example on rotation.
* Provisioning operations are serialised across every `CardProvisioning` instance in the process, so a concurrent call now returns `ProvisioningInProgress` instead of interfering with the in-flight request.
* `CancellationException` is no longer captured and reported as a failure result; cancellation propagates to the caller's coroutine scope.
